              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 5,
                "start": 5
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "The United States contends that the Immigration and Nationality Act\u2019s use of the word \u201cshall\u201d does not create an unyielding mandate to apprehend every non\u2011citizen, and that the Court has repeatedly held that \u201cshall\u201d does not displace background principles of enforcement discretion."
